  "corrections": [
   "tools/jlc_stock.py's placements parser originally took the maximum of every digit run found anywhere in a Parts.md row's Placements/board cell, including digits embedded in an unrelated parenthetical note (e.g. the '11' in 'R11's rotation/encoder/BENCH-source functions'); this inflated the RP2354B's held-parts need from 5 to 55 and wrongly failed rule 6. Fixed to read only the leading count or range at the start of the cell.",
   "tools/jlc_stock.py's Digi-Key lookup treated any non-200 response as 'no match', so six parts whose exact orderable string returns HTTP 404 'Duplicate Products found' (e.g. 74AUP1G32GW,125; SN74LVC1G04DBVR; 74LVC1G175GW,125; SN74AUP1G17DBVR; SN74LVC1G126DBVR) or a differing Digi-Key suffix (BTS7004-1EPP vs Digi-Key's BTS70041EPPXUMA1) were reported as failing when they are in stock. Added a keyword-search fallback that resolves the correct orderable by normalized part-number match.",
   "tools/jlc_stock.py only required a second-vendor (Digi-Key) stock check to pass when the JLCPCB (rule 4) reading had already failed, so a row could pass --check while failing sourcing rule 5 outright. Corrected so the second-vendor gate is checked unconditionally, as the rule requires.",
   "The life-cycle-status extraction used while building Parts.md matched the keyword 'Obsolete' anywhere in a candidate's lifecycle text, which mis-stated INA3221AIRGVR's status as Obsolete from a disclaimer clause ('the page's OBSOLETE mark is another orderable's, not flagged') that says the opposite; corrected to read only the reading's leading clause, giving the true status (Active)."
  ],
